      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.1.1.42 “Traditional Enduro” means Enduro of one or more days of Competition over a natural terrain",
      "text": "1.1.1.42 “Traditional Enduro” means Enduro of one or more days of Competition over a natural terrain \ncourse of up to 7.5 hours duration. The course consists of a number of trail sections between \n5km and 35km in length with time checks at the end of each section. Riders enter the trails three \nper minute and attempt to maintain a pre-determined time allowance on each  section. There are \npenalties for late and early check-in at the Time Checks. There are a number of “Special Tests” \nthroughout the course.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.1.1.43 “Venue” means a permanent or temporary place or facility, which has been approved by the RCB",
      "text": "1.1.1.43 “Venue” means a permanent or temporary place or facility, which has been approved by the RCB \nfor the conduct of Motorcycle Competition.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1 2 INTERPRETATION",
      "text": "1�2               INTERPRETATION",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.2.1 Headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation and, unless the context indicates",
      "text": "1.2.1 Headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation and, unless the context indicates \na contrary intention, “includes” in any form is not a word of limitation, a reference to “month” is to a \ncalendar month, and a reference to “$” or “dollar” is to Australian currency.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1 3 PURPOSE AND AUTHORITY OF GCRS",
      "text": "1�3 PURPOSE AND AUTHORITY OF GCRS",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.3.1.1 The purpose of the GCRs is to regulate and control Motorcycle Competition.",
      "text": "1.3.1.1 The purpose of the GCRs is to regulate and control Motorcycle Competition.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.3.1.2 The GCRs are made under clause 15 of the MA Constitution, are binding on all members of MA",
      "text": "1.3.1.2 The GCRs are made under clause 15 of the MA Constitution, are binding on all members of MA \nand are to be interpreted in accordance with the MA Constitution.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.3.1.3 Any RCB or Promoter organising or any individual participating in an Event is deemed to know",
      "text": "1.3.1.3 Any RCB or Promoter organising or any individual participating in an Event is deemed to know \nand be bound by the GCRs and the SRs together with relevant MA policies including the MA \nAnti-Doping Policy and the National Integrity Framework and undertakes, without reservation to \nsubmit to the authority thereof.\n\n10\n1 JURISDICTION\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.3.2 Recognition of Authority of FIM",
      "text": "1.3.2 Recognition of Authority of FIM",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.3.2.1 In making the GCRs, MA acknowledges and recognises that:",
      "text": "1.3.2.1 In making the GCRs, MA acknowledges and recognises that:\na) FIM is the World Controlling Body of Motorcycle Competition, and\nb) It is desirable that there be consistent standards and rules of Competition at all levels.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1 4 REPEAL OF CURRENT GCRS",
      "text": "1�4 REPEAL OF CURRENT GCRS",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.4.1.1 The GCRs of MA in operation at the date of commencement of these GCRs are hereby repealed",
      "text": "1.4.1.1 The GCRs of MA in operation at the date of commencement of these GCRs are hereby repealed \nbut such repeal will not affect the operation of the repealed GCRs in relation to any Competition \nconducted thereunder.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1 5 BY - LAWS",
      "text": "1�5 BY - LAWS",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.5.1.1 MA may make by-laws which must be consistent with these GCRs, and which may:",
      "text": "1.5.1.1 MA may make by-laws which must be consistent with these GCRs, and which may:\na) Proclaim model SRs,\nb) Prescribe forms and fees as required under the GCRs,\nc) Prescribe fines for any breach of the GCRs,\nd) Prescribe  the requirements for, and conditions of, insurance under the GCRs,\ne) Establish National and State Championships, titled Events, Series, Competitions and \nEvents and for such purposes:\ni)     Define criteria for the eligibility of licensees,\nii)    Define criteria for the eligibility of Motorcycles,\niii) Publish calendars,\niv) Create prizes, trophies and medallions,\nv) Prescribe Competition formats,\nvi) Prescribe traveling and other expenses,\nvii) Attach any relevant FIM rule or regulation.\nf) Prescribe manuals and procedures for the performance by any person or body of any \npower, duty or function under the GCRs,\ng) Provide for the establishment and operation of training and educational courses,\nh) Prescribe the design, function and operation of apparatus, instruments and equipment used \nfor timing, measuring, weighing, counting or calculating,\ni) Prescribe levels of noise, atmospheric and other emissions from Motorcycles,\nj) Prescribe fuel contents and standards,\nk) Prescribe laboratories for fuel testing,\nl) Prescribe track and Venue conditions, designs and standards,\nm) Establish the weights, measurements and other dimensions of Motorcycles, and\nn) Provide for or prescribe such acts, matters or things as shall be necessary for the full and \neffective operation of the GCRs,\no) Prescribe the requirements for obtaining and renewing licences, endorsements and \naccreditations.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.5.1.2 Subject to this GCR, an SCB may make by-laws, which must be consistent with these GCRs and",
      "text": "1.5.1.2 Subject to this GCR, an SCB may make by-laws, which must be consistent with these GCRs and \nconsistent with anything done or made under GCR 1.5.1.1, and which may:\na) Establish State and Territory Championships, titled Events, Series, Competitions and \nEvents for such purposes:\ni)     Publish calendars which do not conflict with any national calendar,\nii) Create prizes, trophies and medallions�\nb) Provide for or prescribe such acts, matters or things as shall be necessary for the full and \neffective operation of by-laws.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.5.1.3 An SCB must, not less than one month after any by-law has been made by that SCB, forward a",
      "text": "1.5.1.3 An SCB must, not less than one month after any by-law has been made by that SCB, forward a \ncopy thereof to the Board.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "1.5.1.4 The Board may amend or revoke any by-law made under the GCRs.",
      "text": "1.5.1.4 The Board may amend or revoke any by-law made under the GCRs.\n\n11\n1 JURISDICTION\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\n\n12",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": "Chapter 2: Administration",
      "text": "2 ADMINISTRATION\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\n2 ADMINISTRATION",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2 1 THE CONTROLLING BODIES",
      "text": "2�1 THE CONTROLLING BODIES",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.1 Administration of Rules",
      "text": "2.1.1 Administration of Rules",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.1.1 Subject to the provisions of the Code, the bodies with authority and responsibility for the",
      "text": "2.1.1.1 Subject to the provisions of the Code, the bodies with authority and responsibility for the \nadministration of rules regulating the conduct of Competitions in all disciplines are as follows:\na) FIM - World Championships and FIM Prize Events as they are defined in the Code,\nb)      MA:\ni)  International events, or Events that connote a national status other than World \nChampionship and FIM Prize Events,\nii) Australian Championships,\niii) MA Series,\niv) Australian Record attempts,\nv) Events which have a course traversing more than one State,\nvi) Support events at World Championships,\nc) SCBs - All other Competitions within the territorial borders of their State unless permission \nhas been granted by the SCB within the territory of the proposed event for another RCB to \npermit the activity.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.2 Specialist Sub-committees",
      "text": "2.1.2 Specialist Sub-committees",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.2.1 An RCB may appoint specialist Sub-committees for the following purposes:",
      "text": "2.1.2.1 An RCB may appoint specialist Sub-committees for the following purposes:\na) To examine any machine to determine if the machine, or the class or group of machines of \nwhich the machine is an example, is eligible to compete,\nb) To issue, in respect of any machine, any logbook or other record of eligibility,\nc) To direct the issue of a replacement logbook for any machine, and\nd) To grant any exemption, in respect of any machine, class or period group of machines, for \nthe use of any part or parts as provided for under these GCRs.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.2.2 The relevant Commission will, unless otherwise determined in by-laws, be the specialist Sub-",
      "text": "2.1.2.2 The relevant Commission will, unless otherwise determined in by-laws, be the specialist Sub-\ncommittee for each SCB.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.2.3 Specialist Sub-committees will be appointed for such term and upon such conditions as the RCB",
      "text": "2.1.2.3 Specialist Sub-committees will be appointed for such term and upon such conditions as the RCB \ndetermines.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.2.4 A specialist Sub-committee may have expertise in more than one discipline of the sport.",
      "text": "2.1.2.4 A specialist Sub-committee may have expertise in more than one discipline of the sport.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.2.5 A determination of a specialist Sub-committee applies to, and binds:",
      "text": "2.1.2.5 A determination of a specialist Sub-committee applies to, and binds:\na) The owner or entrant of any machine,\nb) Any subsequent owner or entrant.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.3 Use of Titles",
      "text": "2.1.3 Use of Titles",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.3.1 The use of any description of an Event which implies a World or Continental status or the use of",
      "text": "2.1.3.1 The use of any description of an Event which implies a World or Continental status or the use of \nthe term International as a title or subtitle is reserved for events which are inscribed in the FIM or \nappropriate Continental Union Calendar.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.3.2 The use of any description of an Event which implies an Australian or National status is reserved",
      "text": "2.1.3.2 The use of any description of an Event which implies an Australian or National status is reserved \nfor events which are administered by MA.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.4 Agreements for Conduct of the Sport",
      "text": "2.1.4 Agreements for Conduct of the Sport",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.4.1 Subject to these GCRs, any RCB may enter into agreements or arrangements with other RCBs,",
      "text": "2.1.4.1 Subject to these GCRs, any RCB may enter into agreements or arrangements with other RCBs, \nor with any Promoter for the conduct of events.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.4.2 If any such agreement or arrangement:",
      "text": "2.1.4.2 If any such agreement or arrangement:\na) Includes FIM, and\nb) Is for the conduct of an event which includes both International and National Competition, \nwhere relevant the GCRs will apply to the National Competition conducted at the event, but \nin all other respects the Code will apply and be binding on all participants.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.5 Conflict between Code and GCRs",
      "text": "2.1.5 Conflict between Code and GCRs",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.1.5.1 If the GCRs and the Code are in conflict in relation to any matter to which both apply, the Code",
      "text": "2.1.5.1 If the GCRs and the Code are in conflict in relation to any matter to which both apply, the Code \nwill prevail. \n\n13\n2 ADMINISTRATION\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2 2 SPORTS DEVELOPMENT LEVY",
      "text": "2�2 SPORTS DEVELOPMENT LEVY",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.2.1 Collection and Distribution",
      "text": "2.2.1 Collection and Distribution",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.2.1.1 MA may establish a Sports Development Levy for any one or more discipline and prescribe the",
      "text": "2.2.1.1 MA may establish a Sports Development Levy for any one or more discipline and prescribe the \namount payable by the Promoter for an Event in that discipline",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.2.1.2 The Promoter of an Event must, within 14 days after Event, pay to MA the prescribed Sports",
      "text": "2.2.1.2 The Promoter of an Event must, within 14 days after Event, pay to MA the prescribed Sports \nDevelopment Levy imposed on takings from:\na) Charges for admission by the public to the Event Venue , and\nb) Sales of programs for the Event.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2 3 SPORTS DEVELOPMENT ACCOUNT",
      "text": "2�3 SPORTS DEVELOPMENT ACCOUNT",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.3.1.1 MA must pay any proceeds it receives from the Sports Development Levy into a Sports",
      "text": "2.3.1.1 MA must pay any proceeds it receives from the Sports Development Levy into a Sports \nDevelopment Account.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.3.1.2 In each year, the Board may determine the purpose for and the amount of any distribution from",
      "text": "2.3.1.2 In each year, the Board may determine the purpose for and the amount of any distribution from \nthe Sports Development Account.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.3.1.3 The Board may impose any conditions on the recipients of grants from the Sports Development",
      "text": "2.3.1.3 The Board may impose any conditions on the recipients of grants from the Sports Development \nAccount.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2 4 OFFICIALS",
      "text": "2�4               OFFICIALS",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.4.1 Powers and Authorities",
      "text": "2.4.1 Powers and Authorities",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.4.1.1 For information regarding the powers and authorities of officials, refer to the MA Officials’ Powers",
      "text": "2.4.1.1 For information regarding the powers and authorities of officials, refer to the MA Officials’ Powers \nand Authorities document, available on the MA website www.ma.org.au.\n2�4�2 Officials Accreditation, Upgrades and Renewals",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.4.2.1 For information regarding officials accreditation, upgrades and renewals, refer to the MA Officials",
      "text": "2.4.2.1 For information regarding officials accreditation, upgrades and renewals, refer to the MA Officials \nAccreditations, Upgrades and Renewals document, available on the MA website www.ma.org.au",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2 5 LICENSING",
      "text": "2�5               LICENSING",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.5.1 Licence Conditions",
      "text": "2.5.1 Licence Conditions",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "2.5.1.1 For all licensing and endorsement requirements, please refer to the MA Licence Conditions and",
      "text": "2.5.1.1 For all licensing and endorsement requirements, please refer to the MA Licence Conditions and \nEndorsements Document available at www.ma.org.au.\nFor information on becoming an Official or to upgrade and/or renew\nyour Officials accreditation, visit the MA Coaching and Officials page \nat www.ma.org.au\n\n14",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": "Chapter 3: Events",
      "text": "3 EVENTS \n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\n3 EVENTS",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3 1 VENUES",
      "text": "3�1               VENUES",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.1 Register of Venues",
      "text": "3.1.1 Register of Venues",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.1.1 Each         SCB must, for its area of responsibility, establish and maintain a register of:",
      "text": "3.1.1.1         Each         SCB must, for its area of responsibility, establish and maintain a register of:\na) Permanent Venues, and\nb) Temporary Venues for special Events which may be altered by the addition, removal or \nmodification of, any one or more Venues.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.2 Track Inspectors",
      "text": "3.1.2 Track Inspectors",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.2.1 For information regarding Track Inspectors, please refer to the MA Officials’ Powers and",
      "text": "3.1.2.1 For information regarding Track Inspectors, please refer to the MA Officials’ Powers and \nAuthorities document, available on the MA website, www.ma.org.au.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.3 The Licensing of Tracks",
      "text": "3.1.3 The Licensing of Tracks",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.3.1 No Venue may be operated without a track licence.",
      "text": "3.1.3.1 No Venue may be operated without a track licence.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.3.2 An application for the issue of a track licence must be in the prescribed form to the RCB",
      "text": "3.1.3.2 An application for the issue of a track licence must be in the prescribed form to the RCB",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.3.3 The RCB may, in respect of a track:",
      "text": "3.1.3.3 The RCB may, in respect of a track:\na) Issue a licence subject to such terms and conditions as it thinks fit or may refuse to issue a \nlicence, and\nb) Revoke or suspend a track licence if the Venue licensee fails to comply with the licence or \nany condition.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.3.4 During each Event the track licence must be prominently displayed in the administration area",
      "text": "3.1.3.4 During each Event the track licence must be prominently displayed in the administration area \nof the Event together with a plan of the Venue and the GPS co-ordinates for the location of the \nVenue.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.3.5 Any support person who enters a Venue or who otherwise participates (in whatever manner",
      "text": "3.1.3.5 Any support person who enters a Venue or who otherwise participates (in whatever manner \nand actively or passively) in an Event is bound by these GCRs and any SRs in force for that \ncompetition.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4 Notices to the Public",
      "text": "3.1.4 Notices to the Public",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4.1 At all Events to which the public have access, other than Events on a public road, the standard",
      "text": "3.1.4.1 At all Events to which the public have access, other than Events on a public road, the standard \nnotice [Notice 4.1] warning the public that a Motorcycle Competition is in progress shall be \nprominently displayed. The sign shall measure 550mm x 450mm, minimum.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4.2 Wherever at such Events, it is considered desirable by the Promoter, or is a condition of the grant",
      "text": "3.1.4.2 Wherever at such Events, it is considered desirable by the Promoter, or is a condition of the grant \nof a track licence that the public shall be excluded from a certain area, the standard form of notice \nprohibiting the public from access to that area [Notice 4.2] shall be prominently displayed. The \nsign shall measure 550mm x 450mm, minimum.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4.3 No other form of notice for warning the public or for prohibiting access to certain areas shall be",
      "text": "3.1.4.3 No other form of notice for warning the public or for prohibiting access to certain areas shall be \nused.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4.4 A sign must be prominently displayed in pit areas [Notice 4.3] warning that the carrying or",
      "text": "3.1.4.4 A sign must be prominently displayed in pit areas [Notice 4.3] warning that the carrying or \nconsumption of alcoholic beverages by all personnel in the area is prohibited. The sign shall \nmeasure 550mm x 450mm, minimum.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4.5 At the entrances to any Venue a Promoter must prominently display the sign entitled ‘Notice’",
      "text": "3.1.4.5 At the entrances to any Venue a Promoter must prominently display the sign entitled ‘Notice’ \n[Notice 4.4]. The sign shall measure 550mm x 450mm, minimum.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4.6 Pit areas must be clearly defined. A Promoter must prominently display the sign [Notice 4.5] at the",
      "text": "3.1.4.6 Pit areas must be clearly defined. A Promoter must prominently display the sign [Notice 4.5] at the \nentrance to the pit area. The sign shall measure 550mm x 450mm, minimum.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4.7 A sign must be prominently displayed in pit areas [Notice 4.6] ‘No Smoking in Pit Area By Order,",
      "text": "3.1.4.7 A sign must be prominently displayed in pit areas [Notice 4.6] ‘No Smoking in Pit Area By Order, \nMA Ltd’. The sign shall measure 550mm x 450mm, minimum. ‘This is a no smoking area’ signs \nmust be placed in grand stands and/or high volume spectator areas [Notice 4.7].",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.1.4.8 A sign must be prominently displayed in pit areas [Notice 4.8] ‘No Open Footwear or Open Toe",
      "text": "3.1.4.8 A sign must be prominently displayed in pit areas [Notice 4.8] ‘No Open Footwear or Open Toe \nShoes to be worn in Pit Area By Order, MA Ltd’. The sign shall measure 550mm x 450mm, \nminimum. \n\n15\n3 EVENTS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3 2 THE PROMOTION AND CONDUCT OF EVENTS",
      "text": "3�2 THE PROMOTION AND CONDUCT OF EVENTS",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.1 Authority to Promote",
      "text": "3.2.1 Authority to Promote",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.1.1 Subject to the GCRs, Events may be promoted or conducted by:",
      "text": "3.2.1.1 Subject to the GCRs, Events may be promoted or conducted by:\na) An RCB, or\nb) A Promoter being either a club affiliated to MA or to an SCB, or a private Promoter being a \nPromoter that is not an affiliated club�",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.1.2 An Event that is to be promoted or conducted by a private Promoter must be the subject of a",
      "text": "3.2.1.2 An Event that is to be promoted or conducted by a private Promoter must be the subject of a \nPromoter Agreement between the RCB and the private Promoter that describes the respective \nduties, responsibilities and liabilities of each party, and imposes on the private Promoter the \nobligation to insure against liability to pay compensation for personal injury, property damage or \nadvertising injury arising out of the private Promoter’s acts or omissions therefrom.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.1.3 SCBs must notify MA of the details of affiliated Promoters within one month of them affiliating.",
      "text": "3.2.1.3 SCBs must notify MA of the details of affiliated Promoters within one month of them affiliating.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.1.4 Where an event that is to be promoted or conducted by a club, such club must be:",
      "text": "3.2.1.4 Where an event that is to be promoted or conducted by a club, such club must be:\na) If an SCB is the RCB, affiliated with the SCB, or\nb) If MA is the RCB, affiliated with MA if they have not already affiliated with an SCB.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.2 Competition Permits",
      "text": "3.2.2 Competition Permits",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.2.1 No Event may be:",
      "text": "3.2.2.1 No Event may be:\na)  Promoted without prior approval from the RCB.\nb)  Conducted without a Competition permit.\nWARNING TO THE PUBLIC\nMotor racing is DANGEROUS, and spectators attending this track do so entirely at their own risk. It is \na condition of admission that all persons having a connection with the promotion, and/or organisation, \nand/or conduct of the meeting, including the owners of the land and the riders and owners of vehicles and \npassengers in the vehicles, are absolved from all liability arising out of the accidents causing damage or \npersonal injury to spectators or ticket holders, except where due care and skill has not been exercised.\nNotice 4.1\nPROHIBITED AREA\nThe Public is not permitted in this area.\nNotice 4.2\nWARNING\nThe carrying or consumption of alcoholic beverages \n in the pit area is prohibited.\nBy Order,\nMotorcycling Australia Ltd\nNotice 4.3\nNOTICE\nNo Animals Allowed.\nGuide Dogs and accredited Assistant Animals \nExcepted.\nMust be kept on a lead (or restrained) at all times.\nBy Order, Motorcycling Australia Ltd.\nNotice 4.4\nThe riding of motorcycles in the pit area is only  \nallowed in marked access lanes.\nBy Order,\nMotorcycling Australia Ltd\nNotice 4.5\nSMOKING PROHIBITIONS\nNo Smoking in Pit Area\nBy Order,\nMotorcycling Australia Ltd\nNotice 4.6\nNotice 4.7\nNo Open Footwear or Open Toe Shoes to \nbe worn in Pit Area\nBy Order,\nMotorcycling Australia Ltd\nNotice 4.8\n\n16\n3 EVENTS \n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.2.2 An application for a Competition permit must be in the prescribed form to the RCB and must:",
      "text": "3.2.2.2 An application for a Competition permit must be in the prescribed form to the RCB and must:\na) Be accompanied by the prescribed fee,\nb) For any Event forming part of an Australian Championship, be submitted at least 12 weeks \nbefore the date set for the Event,\nc) For International Events (i.e. involving licensees from federations other than MA, MA series, \nor National Events with a description implying an Australian or National status, be submitted \nat least eight weeks before the date set for the Event,\nd) For State or Open status Events, be submitted at least eight four weeks before the date set \nfor the Event,\ne) For any other Event, be submitted at least two weeks before the date set for the Event,\nf) Be accompanied by proposed SRs, and\ng) Identify the proposed Venue.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.2.3 An RCB may issue a Competition permit subject to terms and conditions or may refuse to issue a",
      "text": "3.2.2.3 An RCB may issue a Competition permit subject to terms and conditions or may refuse to issue a \npermit.\na) At the time of issue of a Competition permit to a Promoter, the RCB may require the \nPromoter to deposit with the RCB a bond which is:\ni)     Equivalent to the prize money, and/or\nii) An estimate by the RCB of the gate levy payable.\nb) Where a bond is not required, the RCB will assume responsibility for the prize money.\nc) A permit must not be issued unless the Promoter making application is insured to the \nsatisfaction of the RCB.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.2.4 Where any of the conditions of a Competition permit are not satisfied the RCB may revoke the",
      "text": "3.2.2.4 Where any of the conditions of a Competition permit are not satisfied the RCB may revoke the \npermit.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.2.5 The permit for an Event must be prominently displayed in the administration area of the Event.",
      "text": "3.2.2.5 The permit for an Event must be prominently displayed in the administration area of the Event.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.3 Refund of Permit Fees",
      "text": "3.2.3 Refund of Permit Fees",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.3.1 If an Event does not take place, any fee paid for the permit must be repaid unless in the opinion",
      "text": "3.2.3.1 If an Event does not take place, any fee paid for the permit must be repaid unless in the opinion \nof the RCB, the meeting did not take place because of the conduct of the permit holder. In that \nEvent, the RCB may withhold the refund wholly or in part at its discretion.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.4 Forfeiture of Permit",
      "text": "3.2.4 Forfeiture of Permit",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.4.1 A Promoter will be liable to forfeit a permit if the Promoter breaches any of the GCRs, or if a",
      "text": "3.2.4.1 A Promoter will be liable to forfeit a permit if the Promoter breaches any of the GCRs, or if a \nprivate Promoter is in breach of the Promoter Agreement, and in all things done in relation to an \nEvent, must comply with, and is bound by:\na) the GCRs,\nb) All conditions of the permit,\nc) Any SRs, and\nd) MA and governmental Venue standards.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.5 The Appointment of Key Officials",
      "text": "3.2.5 The Appointment of Key Officials",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.5.1 An Event must not take place, and an Event permit is not valid, unless it takes place under the",
      "text": "3.2.5.1         An Event must not take place, and an Event permit is not valid, unless it takes place under the \ndirection and control of the Key Officials.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.5.2 Key Officials for Australian Championships forming a series must:",
      "text": "3.2.5.2         Key Officials for Australian Championships forming a series must:\na) In respect of Stewards, be appointed by MA,\nb) In respect of all other Key Officials, be nominated by the Promoter for approval by MA.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.5.3 Key Officials for Australian Championships which do not form part of a series must:",
      "text": "3.2.5.3         Key Officials for Australian Championships which do not form part of a series must:\na) In respect of Stewards, and Eligibility Scrutineers, be appointed by MA,\nb) In respect of all other Key Officials, be nominated by the Promoter for approval by MA.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.5.4 Key Officials for Events permitted by MA which are not Australian Championships must:",
      "text": "3.2.5.4         Key Officials for Events permitted by MA which are not Australian Championships must:\na) In respect of Stewards, be appointed by MA,\nb) In respect of all other Key Officials, be nominated by the Promoter for approval by MA.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.5.5 Key Officials for Events controlled by SCBs must:",
      "text": "3.2.5.5         Key Officials for Events controlled by SCBs must: \na) In respect of Stewards, be appointed by the SCB,\nb) In respect of all other Key Officials, be nominated by the Promoter for approval by the SCB.\n\n17\n3 EVENTS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.5.6 The Steward of an Event is vested by MA with supreme control and authority over the conduct of",
      "text": "3.2.5.6 The Steward of an Event is vested by MA with supreme control and authority over the conduct of \nall Competition.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.6 Competitions between Categories of Machine",
      "text": "3.2.6 Competitions between Categories of Machine",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.6.1 In respect of any Competition:",
      "text": "3.2.6.1 In respect of any Competition:\na) Unless otherwise provided for by the GCRs or any relevant SRs approved by MA, no two \nmachines of a different category may compete in any Competition,\nb) No Competition may be conducted under the GCRs between a Motorcycle and any other \nvehicle.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.7 Invitations for Entries",
      "text": "3.2.7 Invitations for Entries",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.7.1 A Promoter may invite and receive entries to any Competition authorised by the permit. Every",
      "text": "3.2.7.1 A Promoter may invite and receive entries to any Competition authorised by the permit. Every \ninvitation to enter and every entry form sent out to a potential participant must:\na) Specify the closing date for applications to enter,\nb) Specify the amount of the entry fee,\nc)  Be accompanied by a copy of the SRs for the Event.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.8 Applications for Entries",
      "text": "3.2.8 Applications for Entries",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.8.1 A licence holder wishing to participate in an Event may apply to enter the Event. The application",
      "text": "3.2.8.1 A licence holder wishing to participate in an Event may apply to enter the Event. The application \nmust:\na) Be in the prescribed form and contain the prescribed information,\nb) Be accompanied by the prescribed fee,\nc) If required by the RCB, be accompanied by a medical certificate that the applicant is fit to \nparticipate in the Event,\nd) Contain no false or misleading information,\ne) Comply with the SRs for the Event.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.8.2 The Promoter to whom such an application is submitted may not reject it without the prior",
      "text": "3.2.8.2 The Promoter to whom such an application is submitted may not reject it without the prior \napproval of the RCB. If the application is rejected, the Promoter must inform the applicant of the \nrejection and state the reason for rejection. The applicant can protest the rejection in accordance \nwith the Offences, Protests and Appeals chapter of these GCRs.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.9 Responsibilities of Promoters",
      "text": "3.2.9 Responsibilities of Promoters",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.9.1 A Promoter, on or before the day of the Event must:",
      "text": "3.2.9.1 A Promoter, on or before the day of the Event must:\na) Publish a program which must contain:\ni)     The names of all competitors and the identity of each competitor’s entrant, club and \nState,\nii)    The identification number of each competitor and Motorcycle,\niii) Any applicable starting position and handicap,\niv)    The status and identity of all Key Officials,\nv) All relevant information about the Competitions to be conducted,\nvi) For Australian Championships, a welcome message from an MA Representative,\nvii) A single page ad for MA. MA to provide the artwork.\nb) Provide copies of the program to all Key Officials, entrants and competitors.\nc) Appoint Officials and in so doing may appoint assistant pit and flag marshals who need not \nbe the holders of Officials’ licenses. No assistant pit or flag marshal may carry out any duty \nunless directly supervised by a licensed Official.\nd) Provide fire extinguishers for immediate use at the start area to the satisfaction of the RCB,\ne) Where MA is the RCB, at any Event where speed is the determining factor, provide an \nambulance which is (subject to availability):\ni)     Legally authorised by its relevant State/Territory Government Authority to transport on \npublic roads, under emergency conditions (lights and sirens) any persons to hospital, \nand\nii) Staffed by at least two paramedics who are able to provide advanced life support \ninclusive of providing analgesia.\n\n18\n3 EVENTS \n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\nf) At all other Events where speed is the determining factor provide, to the satisfaction of the \nSCB:\ni)  An ambulance, or\nii) First aid vehicle, or\niii) A medical room, which may be mobile.\ng) Ensure medical facilities are operated by qualified first aid personnel.\nh) Ensure that:\ni)     At Speedway / Track Events spectators are not permitted inside the circuit,\nii) At all other Events spectators are not permitted in areas which may endanger \nthemselves or riders.\niii)    Both the nearest police station and the nearest hospital to the Event are notified that \nthe Event is to take place. This notification must be given at least 21 days prior to the \nEvent.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.9.2 A Promoter must, no more than 21 days after an Event, pay all fees, travel and accommodation",
      "text": "3.2.9.2 A Promoter must, no more than 21 days after an Event, pay all fees, travel and accommodation \nexpenses due to RCBs, riders and Officials in respect of that Event.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.9.3 A Promoter is responsible for the payment of all Officials’ fees and expenses other than the",
      "text": "3.2.9.3 A Promoter is responsible for the payment of all Officials’ fees and expenses other than the \nSteward’s fee.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.9.4 Unless otherwise instructed by the RCB, a Promoter must, no more than 14 days after the results",
      "text": "3.2.9.4 Unless otherwise instructed by the RCB, a Promoter must, no more than 14 days after the results \nhave been declared official, pay all prize monies and prizes due to the riders.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.9.5 At Events where drug or fuel testing has taken place an RCB may instruct the Promoter to delay",
      "text": "3.2.9.5 At Events where drug or fuel testing has taken place an RCB may instruct the Promoter to delay \npayments of prize monies until the results of those tests are published.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.10 Betting at Events",
      "text": "3.2.10 Betting at Events",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.10.1 It is a disciplinary offence for any participant in any Event, including any official, or any rider and",
      "text": "3.2.10.1 It is a disciplinary offence for any participant in any Event, including any official, or any rider and \ntheir crew and their support persons, to bet, gamble or enter into any form of financial speculation \non that Event, or to engage or encourage others to engage in any act of match-fixing.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.11 Results",
      "text": "3.2.11 Results",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.11.1 As soon as practicable and no more than five days after the completion of an Event, the Steward",
      "text": "3.2.11.1 As soon as practicable and no more than five days after the completion of an Event, the Steward \nmust send the results and the Steward’s Event report to the RCB.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.11.2 Unless and until all protests and appeals arising from an Event are finally determined, the results",
      "text": "3.2.11.2 Unless and until all protests and appeals arising from an Event are finally determined, the results \nwill be provisional.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.11.3 In respect of any provisional results, any public announcement or advertisement concerning",
      "text": "3.2.11.3 In respect of any provisional results, any public announcement or advertisement concerning \nthose results must state that they are provisional and are subject to official confirmation.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.11.4 As soon as practicable and no more than five days after the final determination of all protests and",
      "text": "3.2.11.4 As soon as practicable and no more than five days after the final determination of all protests and \nappeals in relation to any Event, the RCB must announce that the results are final.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.11.5 An Event will commence and conclude at the times determined by the Steward.",
      "text": "3.2.11.5 An Event will commence and conclude at the times determined by the Steward.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.12 Results in Australian Championships and MA Series",
      "text": "3.2.12 Results in Australian Championships and MA Series",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.12.1 Results in any Australian titled Event or MA series Event:",
      "text": "3.2.12.1 Results in any Australian titled Event or MA series Event:\na) Must be received by MA by 9am on the Monday next following the Event, and\nb) Must include the names of all finishers in the Event.\n3�2�13          SRs",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.13.1 An RCB may approve SRs, which must be consistent with these GCRs, for the purposes of the",
      "text": "3.2.13.1 An RCB may approve SRs, which must be consistent with these GCRs, for the purposes of the \npromotion and conduct of any Competition.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.13.2 The SRs:",
      "text": "3.2.13.2 The SRs:\na) Have the force and effect of these GCRs,\nb) Must comply, as closely as possible, with the model SRs available on the MA website;\nc) Must be in the prescribed form,\nd) Must be sent to those persons or bodies, whom the RCB considers necessary to enable the \nEvent to be conducted fairly and efficiently, \ne) Must be published and displayed such that Key Officials and competitors have reasonable \naccess to them,\nf) Must not be amended after delivery and publication in accordance with this GCR unless, in \nthe opinion of the Steward, exceptional circumstances arise requiring amendments.\n\n19\n3 EVENTS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\ng)    Entries must not open until such time the SRs have been approved by the relevant \nRCB�",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.13.3 SRs for Events must prescribe:",
      "text": "3.2.13.3 SRs for Events must prescribe:\na) Venue descriptions,\nb)   Dates, times and places of competitions,\nc) Entry times, methods and forms,\nd) Competitor and other numbers and number plates,\ne) Methods of machine examination,\nf) Methods of practicing and qualifying,\ng) Methods of starting and finishing,\nh) Flags and signals,\ni) Competition Officials,\nj) Entry and other fees,\nk) Prizes and trophies,\nl) Competition formats,\nm) Methods of scoring,\nn)      Timetables,\no) Such other facts, matters or things as are necessary to ensure the fair and safe conduct of \ncompetitions.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.13.4 An RCB may approve final instructions, which must be consistent with these GCRs, for the",
      "text": "3.2.13.4 An RCB may approve final instructions, which must be consistent with these GCRs, for the \npurpose of the promotion and conduct of any Event. The final instructions have the force and \neffect of these GCRs.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.13.5 The compulsory riders briefing should follow the MA template – see Officials Documents -",
      "text": "3.2.13.5 The compulsory riders briefing should follow the MA template – see Officials Documents - \nMotorcycling Australia (www.ma.org.au) – and has the force and effect of these GCRs.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.14 SRs for Australian Championships and MA Series",
      "text": "3.2.14 SRs for Australian Championships and MA Series",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.2.14.1 A draft of proposed SRs for an Australian Championship or MA series must be received by MA at",
      "text": "3.2.14.1 A draft of proposed SRs for an Australian Championship or MA series must be received by MA at \nleast three months prior to the date of the Event.\n EVENT PROTOCOLS: AUSTRALIAN CHAMPIONSHIPS AND MA EVENTS",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3 3 MA EVENTS",
      "text": "3�3 MA EVENTS",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.3.1 Events for which MA is the RCB",
      "text": "3.3.1 Events for which MA is the RCB",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.3.1.1 The Events for which MA is the RCB are detailed in GCR 2.1.1.1 (b)",
      "text": "3.3.1.1 The Events for which MA is the RCB are detailed in GCR 2.1.1.1 (b)",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3 4 PROTOCOLS",
      "text": "3�4               PROTOCOLS",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.1 Protocols for MA Series Events and International Meetings",
      "text": "3.4.1 Protocols for MA Series Events and International Meetings",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.2 Where MA is the RCB for a Series or an International Meeting, the Promoter must deal directly",
      "text": "3.4.2 Where MA is the RCB for a Series or an International Meeting, the Promoter must deal directly \nwith MA including as to:\na) The submission of date applications,\nb) The submission of draft SRs,\nc) Payment of fees, bonds and levies.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.2.2 To avoid Event calendar clashes:",
      "text": "3.4.2.2 To avoid Event calendar clashes:\na) MA will advise SCBs of series Event dates and International Meeting dates by 1\nst\n October,\nb) No state or territory championship, or significant event deemed by MA to be in direct \ncompetition with an MA series Event or an International Meeting, may be granted a permit \nby an SCB without the prior approval of MA,\nc) A permit that is not in conformity with item b) of this GCR may be void and any activity \nconducted under that permit uninsured.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.3 Protocols for Australian Championships not forming a Series",
      "text": "3.4.3 Protocols for Australian Championships not forming a Series",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.3.1 Where MA is the RCB for Australian championships not forming a Series, a Promoter may make",
      "text": "3.4.3.1 Where MA is the RCB for Australian championships not forming a Series, a Promoter may make \napplication to MA to host such Championships.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.3.2 The application will include the proposed dates, Venue, Promoter and address the criteria in GCR",
      "text": "3.4.3.2  The application will include the proposed dates, Venue, Promoter and address the criteria in GCR",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4 .",
      "text": "3.4.\n\n20\n3 EVENTS \n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.3.3 The Promoter will provide a copy of the application to the relevant SCB.",
      "text": "3.4.3.3 The Promoter will provide a copy of the application to the relevant SCB.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.3.4 MA will award a Championship to the Promoter who becomes responsible for ensuring the Event is",
      "text": "3.4.3.4 MA will award a Championship to the Promoter who becomes responsible for ensuring the Event is \nconducted to a standard befitting an Australian Championship.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.3.5 MA may require a Promoter to lodge a performance bond which may be totally or partially forfeited",
      "text": "3.4.3.5 MA may require a Promoter to lodge a performance bond which may be totally or partially forfeited \nif key performance criteria are not met.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.3.6 The Promoter is responsible for:",
      "text": "3.4.3.6 The Promoter is responsible for:\na) Providing MA with draft SRs for approval,\nb) Paying MA the performance bond (if any), permit fee and rider insurance levy,\nc)      Publication of SRs,\nd) Providing MA with comprehensive and accurate results by email the day after the Event,\ne) Ensuring there is appropriate promotion and publicity, which is to also incorporate the MA \nlogo and series logo where appropriate. Promotional material includes, but not limited to;\ni)  Electronic Direct Mail (EDMs),\nii)     Posters,\niii)     Websites,\niv) Social Media Posts,\nv) Press Releases,\nvi) Where live streaming is utilised, 1 x MA TV Commercial (TVC). MA to provide TVC.\nf) Ensuring all GCRs governing the administration of Australian Championships are adhered \nto,\ng) Ensuring the prescribed level of medical service is provided.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.3.7 The following issues are key performance criteria Promoters will be assessed on:",
      "text": "3.4.3.7 The following issues are key performance criteria Promoters will be assessed on:\na) Adequate number of officials and other personnel to properly conduct the Event,\nb) The performance of officials,\nc) The appropriate promotion of championships,\nd) Provision of prescribed medical services,\ne) Ensuring there are no date clashes with the championship,\nf) Correct signage,\ng) An effective radio communication system,\nh) An adequate control tower (where appropriate),\ni) A Venue that meets MA standards and local/state government legislative requirements,\nj) Adequate public facilities,\nk) Ensuring the MA logo, flag and trackside signage are displayed as required.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.4 SRs and Entry Forms",
      "text": "3.4.4 SRs and Entry Forms",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.4.1 MA will publish SRs and entry forms on www.ma.org.au for entrants to download.",
      "text": "3.4.4.1 MA will publish SRs and entry forms on www.ma.org.au for entrants to download.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.4.2 SRs and entry forms for:",
      "text": "3.4.4.2 SRs and entry forms for:\na) Series Championships may only be accessed from the MA website or the Promoter,\nb) Stand-alone Championships may be accessed from the MA website, the host SCB or the \nPromoter.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.5 Protest Fees and Fines",
      "text": "3.4.5 Protest Fees and Fines",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.5.1 Protest fees and fines are to be collected by the Steward and paid to MA.",
      "text": "3.4.5.1 Protest fees and fines are to be collected by the Steward and paid to MA.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.6 Venues",
      "text": "3.4.6 Venues",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.6.1 Venues will be licensed by:",
      "text": "3.4.6.1 Venues will be licensed by:\na) FIM – World Championships;\nb) MA – Road Racing Venues;\nc) Stewards – temporary tracks, Trial and Supercross Venues,\nd) SCBs – all other Venues�\n\n21\n3 EVENTS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.7 The Allocation of Australian Championships which do not form a Series",
      "text": "3.4.7 The Allocation of Australian Championships which do not form a Series",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.7.1 In considering applications, MA may have regard to any one or more of the following",
      "text": "3.4.7.1 In considering applications, MA may have regard to any one or more of the following \nconsiderations:\na) The likely level of media exposure of, and public support for, the Event,\nb) The level of support for the discipline by the relevant SCB,\nc)    The regularity and frequency with which State Championships in the discipline are \nheld in the state or territory of the relevant SCB,\nd)    The financial resources of any proposed Promoter of the Event,\ne)    The quality of any proposed Venue,\nf)  The provision of access to any proposed Venue, and accommodation, for spectators.\ng)    The availability of quality Officials,\nh) The previous record of the Promoter in conducting Australian Championships,\ni)  Such other considerations, as MA considers relevant.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.7.2 MA in its absolute discretion may grant the application and may impose such conditions as",
      "text": "3.4.7.2         MA in its absolute discretion may grant the application and may impose such conditions as \nit considers are necessary and reasonable for the fair, efficient and effective conduct of the \nChampionship, or may refuse the application. If the Promoter of an Australian championship fails \nto pay the permit fee or fails to conduct the championship in accordance with the terms of the \ngrant or of these GCRs:\na) MA may offer the Event to another Promoter, and\nb) The performance bond will be forfeited and may be applied by MA in reduction of the permit \nfee payable by such other Promoter.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.8 The Allocation of Australian Championships Forming a Series",
      "text": "3.4.8 The Allocation of Australian Championships Forming a Series",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.8.1 Promoters in each state or territory may apply to MA to host a round of the relevant",
      "text": "3.4.8.1 Promoters in each state or territory may apply to MA to host a round of the relevant \nchampionship.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.9 Promotion of Australian Championships",
      "text": "3.4.9 Promotion of Australian Championships",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.9.1 Programs for Australian Championships must:",
      "text": "3.4.9.1 Programs for Australian Championships must:\na) Indicate on the front cover the nature of the Event,\nb) Give visual prominence to title Events over support Events.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.9.2 At all Australian Championships:",
      "text": "3.4.9.2 At all Australian Championships:\na) An MA flag and banner must be on display at the start or finish line at the Event,\nb) Competitors must place an MA supplied logo on the front number plate of their machines.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.9.3 The MA logo must be displayed following the logo use style-guide issued by MA:",
      "text": "3.4.9.3 The MA logo must be displayed following the logo use style-guide issued by MA:\na) On all publications relating to the Event,\nb) On the front cover of the Event program.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.10 Listing of Australian Championships in State Calendars",
      "text": "3.4.10 Listing of Australian Championships in State Calendars",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "3.4.10.1 The Event calendar of an SCB hosting one or more Australian Championships in any year:",
      "text": "3.4.10.1 The Event calendar of an SCB hosting one or more Australian Championships in any year:\na) Must list each Australian Championship being hosted by that SCB in that year,\nb) Must be sent to MA and all other SCBs by no later than 31\nst\n October of the preceding year.\n\n22",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": "Chapter 4: Alternative Forms of Events",
      "text": "4 ALTERNATIVE FORMS OF EVENTS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\n4 ALTERNATIVE FORMS OF EVENTS",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4 1 ALTERNATIVE ACTIVITIES",
      "text": "4�1 ALTERNATIVE ACTIVITIES",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.1 General",
      "text": "4.1.1 General",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.1.1 Promoters may seek to conduct activities which are outside mainstream Motorcycle Competition",
      "text": "4.1.1.1 Promoters may seek to conduct activities which are outside mainstream Motorcycle Competition \nsuch as:\na) Sand drags, or,\nb) Hill climbs.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.2 Administration of Rules",
      "text": "4.1.2 Administration of Rules",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.2.1 Such Events are to be administered in accordance with GCR 2.1.1.",
      "text": "4.1.2.1  Such Events are to be administered in accordance with GCR 2.1.1.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.3 The Licensing and Powers of Key Officials",
      "text": "4.1.3 The Licensing and Powers of Key Officials",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.3.1 Key Officials are required to be at least Level 3.",
      "text": "4.1.3.1 Key Officials are required to be at least Level 3.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.3.2 The powers, authorities and responsibilities of Officials controlling these activities are those in",
      "text": "4.1.3.2 The powers, authorities and responsibilities of Officials controlling these activities are those in \nGCR 2.4.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.4 The Appointment of Officials",
      "text": "4.1.4 The Appointment of Officials",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.4.1 GCR 3.2.5 applies for the appointment of Officials.?",
      "text": "4.1.4.1 GCR 3.2.5 applies for the appointment of Officials.?",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.5 Venues",
      "text": "4.1.5 Venues",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.5.1 Venues must be inspected and licensed in accordance with GCR 3.1.",
      "text": "4.1.5.1 Venues must be inspected and licensed in accordance with GCR 3.1.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.6 Permits",
      "text": "4.1.6 Permits",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.6.1 An application for a Competition permit must be in the prescribed form to the RCB and must:",
      "text": "4.1.6.1 An application for a Competition permit must be in the prescribed form to the RCB and must:\na) Be accompanied by the prescribed fee and draft SRs,\nb) Be submitted at least 2 months before the date set for the Event,\nc) Be accompanied by evidence that the RCB requirements regarding officials, indemnity \nforms, MA standards and state/territory legislative obligations will be met,\nd) Identify the proposed Venue,\ne) Include details of all ancillary activities.\n4�1�7            SRs",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.7.1 Promoters must include comprehensive details of the proposed Competition in SRs.",
      "text": "4.1.7.1  Promoters must include comprehensive details of the proposed Competition in SRs.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.7.2 SCB must submit the SRs to MA for approval.",
      "text": "4.1.7.2 SCB must submit the SRs to MA for approval.\n4�1�8 Information regarding UTV/SxS recreational/demonstration requirements can be found at www.\nma.org.au",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.9 Licensing of Competitors",
      "text": "4.1.9 Licensing of Competitors",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.9.1 All competitors must be licensed in accordance with the MA Licence Conditions and",
      "text": "4.1.9.1 All competitors must be licensed in accordance with the MA Licence Conditions and \nEndorsements Document.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.10 Technical Specifications",
      "text": "4.1.10 Technical Specifications",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "4.1.10.1 The technical specifications must be approved by MA and be included in the SRs.",
      "text": "4.1.10.1  The technical specifications must be approved by MA and be included in the SRs.\n\n23",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "Chapter 5: Offences, Protests and Appeals",
      "text": "5 OFFENCES, PROTESTS AND APPEALS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\nIn addition to the General Competition RulesIn addition to the General Competition Rules\nplease visit the MA please visit the MA Polices Polices page on the MA websitepage on the MA website\nwww.ma.org.auwww.ma.org.au\n\n24\n5 OFFENCES, PROTESTS AND APPEALS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\nVisit MA’s Calendar for National Events at www.ma.org.au\n5 OFFENCES, PROTESTS AND APPEALS",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5 1 OFFENCES DURING AN EVENT",
      "text": "5�1 OFFENCES DURING AN EVENT",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.1 Prohibited Conduct",
      "text": "5.1.1 Prohibited Conduct",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.1.1 It is an offence if during the course of an Event, any person or entity (including any competitor,",
      "text": "5.1.1.1  It is an offence if during the course of an Event, any person or entity (including any competitor, \nSupport Person, Promoter, entrant, media, member or Official): \na) Breaches, or procures or permits any other person or entity to breach, any GCRs, SRs, MA \npolicy, final instruction or riders briefing instruction; \nb) Acts in a manner prejudicial to the sport, or that brings, or is likely to bring, the sport into \ndisrepute including but not limited to:\ni)  Engaging in unlawful conduct;\nii) Verbally or physically assaulting or intimidating, or being offensive, abusive or \nobstructive toward another person;\nc) Acts in a reckless or dangerous manner while competing; \nd) Disobeys any reasonable directive or instruction of any RCB or Official exercising authority \nunder the GCRs;\ne) Participates or attempts to participate in any Event for which that person or entity has failed \nto complete an entry form, obtain the appropriate licence, or pay entry fees;\nf) Falsifies any document, makes a false or misleading report, or makes a false complaint;",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.1.2 An offence committed by a Support Person may, in addition to any penalty imposed upon that",
      "text": "5.1.1.2  An offence committed by a Support Person may, in addition to any penalty imposed upon that \nSupport Person, result in a penalty being imposed upon the entrant, licensee, competitor or other \nperson associated with such Support Person.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.2 Penalties Applied During Competition",
      "text": "5.1.2 Penalties Applied During Competition",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.2.1 Penalties may be imposed for offences committed during a Competition. In imposing any such",
      "text": "5.1.2.1 Penalties may be imposed for offences committed during a Competition. In imposing any such \npenalty: \na) The rules of natural justice do not apply and the penalty is non-protestable;\nb) The Steward, Referee or Clerk of Course may act on their own initiative or on any \ninformation and in any manner as they think fit having regard to the offending conduct.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.2.2 Such penalty must be capable of being carried out during the Competition in which the offence",
      "text": "5.1.2.2 Such penalty must be capable of being carried out during the Competition in which the offence \noccurred or, if not capable of being carried out during that Competition, must be capable of being \ncarried out during the next Competition involving that competitor.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.3 Determining Offences Committed During an Event",
      "text": "5.1.3 Determining Offences Committed During an Event",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.3.1 This rule 5.1.3 does not apply to an offence dealt with under GCR 5.1.2.",
      "text": "5.1.3.1 This rule 5.1.3 does not apply to an offence dealt with under GCR 5.1.2.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.3.2 Information about any alleged offence under these GCRs committed during an Event should be",
      "text": "5.1.3.2 Information about any alleged offence under these GCRs committed during an Event should be \ndirected to the Clerk of Course.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.3.3 Upon receipt of information of an alleged offence under these GCRs, the Clerk of Course should",
      "text": "5.1.3.3  Upon receipt of information of an alleged offence under these GCRs, the Clerk of Course should \ndetermine if such information justifies initiating a prosecution.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.3.4 A prosecution for any alleged offence under these GCRs committed during an Event must be",
      "text": "5.1.3.4 A prosecution for any alleged offence under these GCRs committed during an Event must be \ninitiated by the laying of charges against the offender, and be communicated to the offender, \nduring the Event.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.3.5 Any such prosecution:",
      "text": "5.1.3.5 Any such prosecution:\na) Should preferably be initiated by the Clerk of Course;\nb) If initiated by the Steward, must be referred to, and be actioned by the Clerk of Course in \naccordance with this rule;\nc) Should be investigated and determined by the Clerk of Course and, if proven, a penalty \nshould be imposed by the Clerk of Course; \nd) If, in the exceptional circumstances that the Clerk of Course is unable or unwilling to initiate, \nInvestigate and/or determine a prosecution, such prosecution will be referred to the Steward \nto be investigated and if proven, determined for the imposition of a penalty.\n\n25\n5 OFFENCES, PROTESTS AND APPEALS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.3.6 In determining an alleged offence and prior to imposing any penalty:",
      "text": "5.1.3.6  In determining an alleged offence and prior to imposing any penalty:\na) The Clerk of Course (or Steward if acting pursuant to GCR 5.1.3.5 d) may act on their own \ninitiative and act on such information and in such manner as they think fit having regard to \nthe offending conduct;\nb) No person or entity may be represented by a legal practitioner or other advocate;\nc) No penalty may be imposed unless and until the offender has been given the opportunity to \nmake representations as to the nature and circumstances of the offence.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.4 Penalties that may be Imposed by the Clerk of Course or Steward",
      "text": "5.1.4 Penalties that may be Imposed by the Clerk of Course or Steward",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.4.1 The Clerk of Course may impose the following penalties for any offence committed under the",
      "text": "5.1.4.1  The Clerk of Course may impose the following penalties for any offence committed under the \nGCRs: \na) A reprimand;\nb) A fine no greater than $2,000 payable to the RCB; \nc) Relegation or drop of position;\nd) A time or points penalty;\ne)      Exclusion;\nf) Removal or ejection from the Venue.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.4.2 The Steward may impose the following penalties for any offence committed under the GCRs:",
      "text": "5.1.4.2 The Steward may impose the following penalties for any offence committed under the GCRs: \na) A reprimand;\nb) A fine no greater than $4,000 payable to the RCB; \nc) Relegation or drop of position;\nd) A time or points penalty;\ne)      Exclusion;\nf) Suspension of no more than six (6) months;\ng) Removal or ejection from the Venue.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.5 Penalties to be Notified to Offender",
      "text": "5.1.5 Penalties to be Notified to Offender",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.5.1 The Clerk of Course or Steward imposing the penalty must, as soon as practicable after",
      "text": "5.1.5.1 The Clerk of Course or Steward imposing the penalty must, as soon as practicable after \ndetermining the penalty, and wherever possible during the Event, inform the offender and their \nteam (if applicable) of the penalty imposed;",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.5.2 A decision to impose a penalty does not come into effect unless and until it is notified to the",
      "text": "5.1.5.2 A decision to impose a penalty does not come into effect unless and until it is notified to the \noffender or to their team (if applicable).",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.6 Right of Protest",
      "text": "5.1.6 Right of Protest",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.6.1 There is no right of protest against, or appeal from, a decision to impose a penalty for an offence",
      "text": "5.1.6.1 There is no right of protest against, or appeal from, a decision to impose a penalty for an offence \ncommitted during Competition.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.6.2 With the exception of penalties imposed during Competition, any entrant or competitor may",
      "text": "5.1.6.2 With the exception of penalties imposed during Competition, any entrant or competitor may \nprotest: \na) Against a decision to reject an application by a competition licence holder to compete in any \nCompetition;\nb) Against a decision, action or determination of any Official;\nc) Against the action or conduct of any other competitor, Support Person, Promoter, entrant or \nOfficial during an Event. \n\n26\n5 OFFENCES, PROTESTS AND APPEALS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.6.3 Any protest must:",
      "text": "5.1.6.3 Any protest must: \na) Be in writing, preferably on the prescribed protest form available from the Race Secretary \nor at www.ma.org.au, and contain sufficient information to convey to the Steward a clear \nunderstanding of what is in dispute. Where, in the opinion of the Steward, a protest does \nnot so contain sufficient information, the Steward may decline to accept or act upon such \nprotest.\nb) Be accompanied by the prescribed fee of $100 (plus the applicable bond under GCR 5.1.7 \nwhere the protest involves the measurement of an engine or component of an engine) \nwhich will be refunded if the protest is upheld;\nc) Be received by the Clerk of Course and conveyed to the Steward;\nd) Comply with the following time limits: \ni)  For a protest under sub-Rules a) and b) of the previous GCR, thirty (30) minutes after \nbeing informed of the decision;\nii) For a protest under sub-Rule c) of the previous GCR being a Speedway or Supercross \nEvent, within five (5) minutes after the finish of the Competition where the action or \nconduct took place, or for any other Event within thirty (30) minutes of such action or \nconduct.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.6.4 . The following additional requirements apply to all competitors who are under the age of 16 years",
      "text": "5.1.6.4. The following additional requirements apply to all competitors who are under the age of 16 years \nand seeking to protest the action or conduct of any other competitor, Official or Support Person \nduring Competition: \na) A protest may only be made by a competitor; \nb) The competitor must indicate the intent to protest to an Official prior to returning to the pits;\nc) The Clerk of Course must designate an area, to be announced at the riders’ briefing and \nto be marked by a purple flag, where an Official must be present to note any indications of \nprotest;\nd) No discussion on the content of the protest may take place at the marked position; and\ne) A competitor who indicates an intent to protest must return to the pits and present the \nprotest to the Clerk of Course within the time limits referred to in the previous rule.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.7 Technical Protests (Engines)",
      "text": "5.1.7 Technical Protests (Engines)",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.7.1 If an engine, or component of an engine, is to be measured for the purposes of a technical",
      "text": "5.1.7.1 If an engine, or component of an engine, is to be measured for the purposes of a technical \nprotest, the protesting party must, in addition to payment of the protest fee, submit a $500 bond.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.7.2 In addition to the matters the Steward must take into account under GCR 5.1.8.3, when",
      "text": "5.1.7.2 In addition to the matters the Steward must take into account under GCR 5.1.8.3, when \ndetermining a technical protest the Steward shall have regard to the measurements recorded in \nthe Measurer’s report.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.7.3 Where the Steward determines that the measured machine:",
      "text": "5.1.7.3 Where the Steward determines that the measured machine:\na) Is ineligible, the bond and the protest fee will be refunded;  \nb) Is eligible, the bond will be forfeited to the party whose engine was measured and the \nprotest fee remitted to the RCB.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.7.4 There is no right of appeal from the Steward’s determination of a technical protest on the basis of",
      "text": "5.1.7.4 There is no right of appeal from the Steward’s determination of a technical protest on the basis of \nany alleged errors in the measurements recorded in the Measurer’s report.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.8 Protest Hearings",
      "text": "5.1.8 Protest Hearings",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.8.1 A Steward must conduct a hearing to determine any protest and must notify the outcome to the",
      "text": "5.1.8.1 A Steward must conduct a hearing to determine any protest and must notify the outcome to the \nprotester, and any other person with a material interest in the protest. Such hearing, and the \nnotification of outcome, must take place during the Event. Only in exceptional circumstances may \nthe Steward defer the hearing and/or the notification of outcome, and then only for such time as \nthe RCB deems reasonable.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.8.2 Only in exceptional circumstances of a Steward being unable to fulfil their duty under the previous",
      "text": "5.1.8.2 Only in exceptional circumstances of a Steward being unable to fulfil their duty under the previous \nGCR, may a Steward refer any question raised in any protest, or the protest itself, to the RCB, in \nwhich case the Steward must as soon as practicable: \na) Notify such referral to the protester, and to any other person with a material interest in the \nprotest;\nb) Provide to the RCB all evidence and exhibits submitted to the Steward in relation to that \nprotest;\nc) Comply with all directions and instructions of the RCB. \n\n27\n5 OFFENCES, PROTESTS AND APPEALS\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.8.3 In hearing and determining any protest, a Steward must:",
      "text": "5.1.8.3 In hearing and determining any protest, a Steward must: \na) Ensure the protester and any other person with a material interest in the outcome of the \nprotest be given reasonable notice of the date, time and place fixed for the hearing;\nb) Apply the principles of natural justice, noting however that,\ni)  No person or entity may be represented by a legal practitioner or other advocate. \nii) The rules of evidence do not apply, and the Steward may be informed of facts in such \nmanner as the Steward thinks fit; and\niii) The protest must be determined on the balance of probabilities where the Steward is \nsatisfied that on the evidence the alleged fact or matter is more probable than not;\nc) Provide their determination of the protest in writing to the protestor and to any other person \nwith a material interest in the determination.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "5.1.8.4 A Steward may:",
      "text": "5.1.8.4 A Steward may: \na) Direct any reasonable alteration or modification to any track or course;\nb) Alter or amend any program;\nc) Vary or overrule any decision or direction of an Official or substitute such decision with \nanother decision with or without conditions;\nd) Give such directions, instructions or orders as the Steward thinks fit for the efficient and fair \nconduct of any Competition;\ne) Alter, vary or amend the result of, or prize for, any Competition;\nf) Do whatever is necessary for the proper consideration of the protest.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
