      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 26 PERIOD 6 SIDECARS AND CYCLECARS 85",
      "text": "7�26 PERIOD 6 SIDECARS AND CYCLECARS � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � � �85\nWant to buy a riding licence, enter an Event or become a Coach/Official?\nVisit RIDERNET\n\n65\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\nAPPLICATION OF CHAPTER\nThe following GCRs governing Historic Road Racing Motorcycles are written to facilitate the organisation of \nuniform and fair Competition.\nThe express purpose of these GCRs is to ensure the Motorcycles are in a condition that is visually compatible \nwith the period of racing being portrayed. These GCRs are to be interpreted so as to ensure that Motorcycles \nare presented in the spirit of the period. All Machines should be prepared to a high standard of cosmetic \nappearance.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "SECTION 7A: AUSTRALIAN CHAMPIONSHIPS AND COMPETITION CLASSES",
      "text": "SECTION 7A: AUSTRALIAN CHAMPIONSHIPS AND COMPETITION CLASSES",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 1 AUSTRALIAN HISTORIC ROAD RACE MATRIX",
      "text": "7�1    AUSTRALIAN HISTORIC ROAD RACE  MATRIX\nHISTORIC ROAD RACINGP1P2P3P4P5P6P7\nUltra-Lightweight/ Solo Up to 125ccCC-CCCCACACAC\nLightweight/ Solo 132cc to 250ccCC-ACACACACAC\nJunior/ Solo 263cc to 350cc CC-ACACAC--\nSenior/ Solo 368cc to 500ccCC-ACACAC--\nSenior/ Solo 263cc to 500cc-----ACAC\nUnlimited/ Solo 526cc to 1300ccCC-ACACAC--\nSidecar: Up to 650ccCCCCACACACAC-\nSidecar: Up to 1300ccCCCCACACACAC-\nJunior/ Solo: Up to 350cc-CC-----\nSenior/ Solo: Up to 500cc-AC-----\nUnlimited/ Solo: 368cc to 1300cc-AC-----\n700/ Solo: 526cc to 700cc\nNote: This class is for push rod engines only.\nThere is no capacity tolerance.\n--AC---\n750/ Solo: 526cc to 750cc---ACAC--\n250 Production Solo 250cc\nNote: Machine must have either a compliance plate \nfitted  or  supporting  documentation  of  the  year  of \nmanufacture. \n-----ACAC\nFormula  750/Solo:  526cc  to  750cc  4-cylinder  and  \n750cc to 1000cc 2-cylinder\n-----AC-\nFormula 1300/ Solo: 788cc to 1300cc-----AC-\n600 Supersport: Production based machines of up \nto 600cc 4-cylinder or 750cc 2-cylinder\nAC\nSuperbike: 4 Stroke Production based machines of \n600 to 750cc 4-cylinder, 600 to 900cc 3-cylinder or \n1000cc 2-cylinder\nAC\nProduction Superbike: 4 Stroke machines greater \nthan 700cc and no greater than 1000cc\nAC\n7�1�1 Historic Matrix Legend\n7�1�1�1 AC = Australian Championship\n CC = Competition Classes",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.1.1.2 Any class that is an Australian Championship (AC), is also a Competition Class (CC).",
      "text": "7.1.1.2 Any class that is an Australian Championship (AC), is also a Competition Class (CC).\n\n66\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\n7�1�3            Periods",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.1.3.1 For the purposes of determining eligibility, Machines are categorised as follows:",
      "text": "7.1.3.1 For the purposes of determining eligibility, Machines are categorised as follows:\nPERIODNAMEDATE RANGES\nP1VeteranUp to 31st December 1919\nP2Vintage1st January 1920 to 31st December 1945\nP3Classic1st January 1946 to 31st December 1962\nP4Post Classic1st January 1963 to 31st December 1972\nP5Forgotten Era1st January 1973 to 31st December 1982\nP6New Era1st January 1983 to 31st December 1990\nP7Golden Era1st January 1991 to 31st December 1999",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 2 CHAMPIONSHIP MEDALLIONS AND TROPHIES",
      "text": "7�2 CHAMPIONSHIP MEDALLIONS AND TROPHIES\n7�2�1 Individual Competitions",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.2.1.1 MA medallions will be presented to the 1st, 2nd and 3rd placed riders in each Championship solo",
      "text": "7.2.1.1 MA medallions will be presented to the 1st, 2nd and 3rd placed riders in each Championship solo \nclass and 1st, 2nd and 3rd placed rider and passenger in the Championship sidecar class at all \nAustralian Championship Events.\n7�2�2 All Competitions",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.2.2.1 At least the first three place getters in any Australian Championship Event must be awarded",
      "text": "7.2.2.1 At least the first three place getters in any Australian Championship Event must be awarded \na sash or similar permanent memento of the achievement by the Promoter, irrespective of MA \nawards.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.2.2.2 Medallions and points will be awarded in all Australian Championships where there are:",
      "text": "7.2.2.2 Medallions and points will be awarded in all Australian Championships where there are:\na) Ten or more entries for all solo classes, who actually participate in practice, qualifying or \nRaces, \nb) Six or more entries for Period 2, 3 & 4 solo classes, who actually participate in practice, \nqualifying or Races,\nc) Six or more entries for sidecar classes, who actually participate in practice, qualifying or \nRaces.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "SECTION 7B: COMPETITION RULES",
      "text": "SECTION 7B: COMPETITION RULES",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 3 ELIGIBILITY: GENERAL",
      "text": "7�3 ELIGIBILITY: GENERAL",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.3.1.1 No person may participate in any Competition, unless and until that person’s protective clothing/",
      "text": "7.3.1.1 No person may participate in any Competition, unless and until that person’s protective clothing/\nequipment and Machine have been examined and approved by the Technical Officer for that \nCompetition.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.3.1.2 At technical inspection, competitors must produce documents or other evidence as required to",
      "text": "7.3.1.2 At technical inspection, competitors must produce documents or other evidence as required to \nverify engine and frame identity.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.3.1.3 The onus of proving that a competitor, and the competitor’s Machine and protective clothing/",
      "text": "7.3.1.3 The onus of proving that a competitor, and the competitor’s Machine and protective clothing/\nequipment, are eligible to compete, is on the person seeking to prove it.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.3.1.4 In the interpretation of any GCR relating to the design requirements for any Machine or class of",
      "text": "7.3.1.4 In the interpretation of any GCR relating to the design requirements for any Machine or class of \nMachines, reference may be made to relevant diagrams appearing in these GCRs.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 4 ELIGIBILITY: MACHINES",
      "text": "7�4 ELIGIBILITY: MACHINES",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.1.1 Machines are eligible to enter:",
      "text": "7.4.1.1 Machines are eligible to enter:\na) The capacity and era class period as shown in the Machine’s log book, and\nb) The next capacity class in that era as per the Historic Matrix 7.1, with the exception of \nPeriod 6 & 7 250cc Production Machines and Lightweight Machines, which cannot enter \nthe next capacity class if they wish to enter both the Period 6 or 7 250 Production class and \nLightweight class,\nc) Unlimited class Machines may enter the next era but must run as per the GCRs of the log \nbook era,\nd) If a machine is entered into another class as per above, the machine must run under \nthe rules of the log booked period/class for that machine�\n\n67\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.1.2 Period 3 500cc Machines are not allowed to compete in the 700 class.",
      "text": "7.4.1.2 Period 3 500cc Machines are not allowed to compete in the 700 class.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.1.3 In cases where classes are combined to be run concurrently in the same Race, points shall only",
      "text": "7.4.1.3 In cases where classes are combined to be run concurrently in the same Race, points shall only \nbe awarded for the class for which the Machine holds an eligible logbook.\n7�4�1�4 Eligibility Period 7\n Rules 7.14.1.3, 7.14.1.4 a), 7.14.1.5 & 7.14.1.8 must be applied to Period 7 Production Superbike \n& 600 Supersport, Superbike and 250 Production machine models manufactured as Year Model \n(YM) 1991 to YM 1999 and produced between the 1st of January 1991 and the 31st of December \n1999 only.\n7�4�2 Log Books",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.2.1 Log books are mandatory for Historic Road Racing Competitions.",
      "text": "7.4.2.1 Log books are mandatory for Historic Road Racing Competitions.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.2.2 With the exception of Machines covered by GCR 7.4.3, Machines that do not hold a log book",
      "text": "7.4.2.2 With the exception of Machines covered by GCR 7.4.3, Machines that do not hold a log book \ncannot compete.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.2.3 Log book application forms are available from the MA website, www.ma.org.au.",
      "text": "7.4.2.3 Log book application forms are available from the MA website, www.ma.org.au.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.2.4 To assist in the issuing of a logbook upon completion of the Machine, before commencing the",
      "text": "7.4.2.4 To assist in the issuing of a logbook upon completion of the Machine, before commencing the \nbuilding of a Machine that consists primarily of replicated parts, plans and specifications may be \nsubmitted to MA for interim approval. Application forms for this purpose are available from www.\nma.org.au.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.2.5 Issuing of a log book is regarded as prima facie acceptance by MA of proof of eligibility of",
      "text": "7.4.2.5 Issuing of a log book is regarded as prima facie acceptance by MA of proof of eligibility of \nMachines and modifications as presented. This does not remove the rights of challenge or \nprotest.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.2.6 Log books must:",
      "text": "7.4.2.6 Log books must:\na) Be produced by the entrant at technical inspection,\nb) Be available for presentation at any other time during the Event,\nc) Contain provision for Eligibility Scrutineers to record any alterations or changes to the \nMachine.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.2.7 Changes to major components must be approved by the:",
      "text": "7.4.2.7 Changes to major components must be approved by the:\na) Historic Road Race Commission and recorded in a revised Historic Log Book, or, \nb) Clerk of Course and/or Eligibility Scrutineer at an Event and recorded in the existing Historic \nLog Book. \n7�4�3 International Competitors",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.3.1 Bona fide International competitors riding Machines from countries other than Australia do not",
      "text": "7.4.3.1 Bona fide International competitors riding Machines from countries other than Australia do not \nrequire a log book, but are required to complete an Overseas Usage form and approval to be \ngranted by MA.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.4.3.2 Overseas competitors’ Machines must comply with either their own Competition rules or those of",
      "text": "7.4.3.2 Overseas competitors’ Machines must comply with either their own Competition rules or those of \nAustralia, and not be a combination of both to gain a competitive advantage.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 5 GENERAL RULES",
      "text": "7�5 GENERAL RULES\n7�5�1            Homologation",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.5.1.1 For any Competition, MA may require that any Machine, or any part of a Machine, including tyres,",
      "text": "7.5.1.1 For any Competition, MA may require that any Machine, or any part of a Machine, including tyres, \nbe homologated. For homologation details, contact MA.\n7�5�2            Cameras",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.5.2.1 Cameras may be fitted to the Motorcycle provided they are securely mounted. Camera mounts",
      "text": "7.5.2.1 Cameras may be fitted to the Motorcycle provided they are securely mounted. Camera mounts \nare subject to approval by the Chief Technical Officer. Helmet cameras are not permitted unless \nthe camera is integrated into the helmet, by design of the manufacturer.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 6 PROTECTIVE CLOTHING AND HELMETS",
      "text": "7�6 PROTECTIVE CLOTHING AND HELMETS",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.6.1.1 No competitor may practice, start or compete in any Historic Road Racing Competition unless",
      "text": "7.6.1.1 No competitor may practice, start or compete in any Historic Road Racing Competition unless \nwearing the protective equipment and clothing as outlined in Appendix A: Protective Clothing and \nEquipment.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 7 MACHINE AND RIDER IDENTIFICATION",
      "text": "7�7 MACHINE AND RIDER IDENTIFICATION\n7�7�1 Number Plates",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.1.1 For all Competitions three number plates must be fitted – one at the front and one on each side.",
      "text": "7.7.1.1 For all Competitions three number plates must be fitted – one at the front and one on each side.\n\n68\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.1.2 Number plates must:",
      "text": "7.7.1.2 Number plates must:\na) Be produced to a matte finish,\nb) Where they are not an integral part of the Machine or streamlining and are under 1.6mm in \nthickness, have rolled or wired edges,\nc) In the case of rectangular plates, have the corners formed to a 38mm radius,\nd) In the case of bolt-on number plates, be made from a rigid material with minimum \ndimensions of 235mm height and 285mm width; and\ne) In the case of sidecars, be positioned so that they are visible from the front and each side of \nthe sidecar.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.1.3 Front number plates must have figures that are clearly visible at a distance of 20 metres and a",
      "text": "7.7.1.3 Front number plates must have figures that are clearly visible at a distance of 20 metres and a \nsolid border 10mm wide.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.1.4 Side number plates must:",
      "text": "7.7.1.4 Side number plates must:\na) Be fitted above a horizontal line drawn through the rear axle,\nb) Be fitted so that the front edge of the plate is behind a vertical line drawn at 200mm to the \nrear of the rider’s footrest.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.1.5 Number backgrounds on side number plates may be an integral part of the rear seat section or",
      "text": "7.7.1.5 Number backgrounds on side number plates may be an integral part of the rear seat section or \nfairing.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.1.6 Advertising must be at least 25mm clear of the background of a number plate background and",
      "text": "7.7.1.6 Advertising must be at least 25mm clear of the background of a number plate background and \nthe rider’s name by either a gap or a contrasting colour strip unless the advertising is an integral \npart of the back-plate cover. \n7�7�2 Number Plate Colours",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.2.1 Colours must be as follows:",
      "text": "7.7.2.1 Colours must be as follows:\nCAPACITY/ CLASSBACKGROUND COLOURFIGURE COLOUR\nUp to 125ccBlackWhite\n126cc to 250ccDark GreenWhite\n251cc to 350ccMid BlueWhite\n351cc to 500ccCanary YellowBlack\n501cc to 750ccWhiteBlack\n750cc to 1000 (Formula 750 only)WhiteBlack\n751cc and overMail Box RedWhite\nUp to 500cc SidecarCanary YellowBlack\nOver 500cc SidecarWhiteBlack\n7�7�3 Number Plate Figures",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.3.1 Font style is free; however, the onus for legibility rests with the entrant.",
      "text": "7.7.3.1 Font style is free; however, the onus for legibility rests with the entrant.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.7.3.2 Figures must be clearly legible, the minimum dimensions being:",
      "text": "7.7.3.2 Figures must be clearly legible, the minimum dimensions being: \nDIMENSIONMEASUREMENT (mm)\nHeight140\nWidth of each figure75\nSpace between figures25\nSpace between figures and edge of plate12",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 8 RACE EVENT PROTOCOLS",
      "text": "7�8 RACE EVENT PROTOCOLS\n7�8�1 Flags and Signals",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.1.1 The minimum dimensions of all flags must be 500mm x 500mm.",
      "text": "7.8.1.1 The minimum dimensions of all flags must be 500mm x 500mm.\n\n69\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.1.2 Track flags and signals as per Appendix B: Flags & Signals.",
      "text": "7.8.1.2 Track flags and signals as per Appendix B: Flags & Signals.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.1.3 The National flag signifying the start of a Competition may be replaced by a light signal.",
      "text": "7.8.1.3 The National flag signifying the start of a Competition may be replaced by a light signal.\n7�8�2 Measurement at Events",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.2.1 A Steward of an Event may direct the measurement of the capacity of the engine of any Machine,",
      "text": "7.8.2.1 A Steward of an Event may direct the measurement of the capacity of the engine of any Machine, \nto be carried out at the conclusion of the Event. Until the measurement is completed the Machine \nmust remain under the control of the RCB.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.2.2 If an engine is measured at the request of a rider or entrant, that rider or entrant is liable for the",
      "text": "7.8.2.2 If an engine is measured at the request of a rider or entrant, that rider or entrant is liable for the \ncost of the measurement.\n7�8�3 Measurement: All Australian and State Championship Events",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.3.1 All Machines must have provision for the placement of sealing wire.",
      "text": "7.8.3.1 All Machines must have provision for the placement of sealing wire.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.3.2 An entrant may request that the entrant’s Machine be measured and sealed before the Event.",
      "text": "7.8.3.2 An entrant may request that the entrant’s Machine be measured and sealed before the Event. \nAs soon as practicable after receiving the request the measurer for the Event must measure and \nseal the Machine. Any Machine examined under this GCR may, on application by the entrant, at \nthe discretion of the measurer, be exempted from further examination at the Event.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.3.3 The 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 4th placed Machines must be impounded for a period of 30 minutes",
      "text": "7.8.3.3 The 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 4th placed Machines must be impounded for a period of 30 minutes \nimmediately following the Race, pending any protest, and the Race result will be provisional,\na) At the conclusion of that period, if no protest is received, the result will be final,\nb) If any such Machine is to be ridden in another Competition within that period, that Machine \nmust be sealed before being returned to the competitor for that Competition,\nc) If no protest is received within that period, the seals may be removed.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.3.4 Any Machine sealed as the result of a protest may only be measured by a Measurer. All",
      "text": "7.8.3.4 Any Machine sealed as the result of a protest may only be measured by a Measurer. All \nMeasurer’s reports, together with the seals, must be delivered to the RCB within 21 days after the \nEvent.\n7�8�4            Starts",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.4.1 All competitors must, in relation to the start of any Competition, comply with directions issued by,",
      "text": "7.8.4.1 All competitors must, in relation to the start of any Competition, comply with directions issued by, \nand under the authority of, the starter. For such purposes the starter, on the instructions of a Key \nOfficial, may:\na) Delay a start,\nb) Direct a Re-start,\nc) Direct a competitor to start from:\ni)  The back of the starting grid,\nii) The pit lane,\niii)    The rear of the field, or\niv) Such other position as shall be required for the safe, fair and orderly start of the \nCompetition.\nd) Exclude a competitor who is late for the start.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.4.2 The method of starting will be as prescribed by SRs.",
      "text": "7.8.4.2 The method of starting will be as prescribed by SRs.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.4.3 The start of a Competition occurs when the order to start is given.",
      "text": "7.8.4.3 The start of a Competition occurs when the order to start is given.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.4.4 No rider may start a Competition after the point where the lead rider has crossed the finish line to",
      "text": "7.8.4.4 No rider may start a Competition after the point where the lead rider has crossed the finish line to \ncomplete the first racing lap. \n7�8�5            Finishes",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.5.1 For Races:",
      "text": "7.8.5.1 For Races:\na) A chequered flag must be displayed to each competitor as each crosses the line, with the \nflag being displayed:\ni)     To the first to complete the Race, who will, subject to the results of any protests, be the \nwinner, and\nii) Thereafter to each competitor who:\n• Has completed not less than 75% of the Race distance,\n• Is still competing in the Race on the race track on the lap in which the \nchequered flag is displayed to the winner, with the sequence of completion of \nRace being the determinant of placings.\n\n70\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\nb) The finish of the Race occurs when the flag is displayed to the last competitor under GCR",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.5.1 a),",
      "text": "7.8.5.1 a),\nc) The finish occurs for each Machine when the foremost part of the Machine crosses the line,\nd) Where there are two competitors required to be on one Machine together, both must finish \nthe Race in contact with the Machine. On a solo Machine, the competitor must finish the \nRace in contact with the Machine,\ne) In case of a dead heat between competitors for a place:\ni)  The places and the awards for those places will be combined,\nii) The participants in the dead heat will share the places and awards equally,\niii) The remaining places will be relegated by the number of participants in the dead heat.\n7�8�6 Stopping Events",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.6.1 Where an incident causes a Race to be stopped, the Steward or Clerk of Course may declare the",
      "text": "7.8.6.1 Where an incident causes a Race to be stopped, the Steward or Clerk of Course may declare the \nRace complete if at least two thirds of the Race distance or time, whichever is the less, has been \nrun.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.6.2 The results established after the review of the incident by the Clerk of Course and so declared will",
      "text": "7.8.6.2 The results established after the review of the incident by the Clerk of Course and so declared will \nbe based on the finishing order of riders recorded on the same lap as the leader, followed by the \nfinishing order of those completing the previous lap, but may Exclude those competitors who:\na) Are proven to have been the cause of the incident, or\nb) Having been involved in the incident, could not continue in the Race.\n7�8�7 Stopping and Re-Running Competitions",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.7.1 The Steward or Clerk of Course who has Excluded a competitor for unfair conduct and considers",
      "text": "7.8.7.1 The Steward or Clerk of Course who has Excluded a competitor for unfair conduct and considers \nthat such conduct has:\na) Given an advantage to the team of which the offender is a member, or\nb) In the case of a non-team Competition, jeopardised the fair chances of one or more of the \nother competitors in the Competition, \n may declare the Competition void and order a Re-run.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.7.2 If the Competition continues, any competitor unable to cross the finish line as a result of such",
      "text": "7.8.7.2 If the Competition continues, any competitor unable to cross the finish line as a result of such \nconduct on the part of the Excluded competitor may be deemed to have finished the Competition \nin the place:\na) Held immediately before such conduct, or\nb) Having regard to any advancement in placing following the exclusion, in some other place.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.7.3 A Steward or Clerk of Course may stop a Competition and order it to be Re-run if it would be",
      "text": "7.8.7.3 A Steward or Clerk of Course may stop a Competition and order it to be Re-run if it would be \ndangerous for it to continue.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.7.4 In any Re-run:",
      "text": "7.8.7.4 In any Re-run:\na) Any competitor who:\ni)  Fell in the stopped Competition as a result of having been fouled,\nii) Intentionally laid down his or her their Machine in the interests of safety, or\niii) Left the course in the interests of safety,\nmay participate.\nb) Any competitor who:\ni)  Caused or contributed to the Competition being stopped,\nii) Failed to start in,\niii) Retired from,\niv) Was Excluded from,\nv) Had been lapped during the course of the stopped Competition,\nmay not participate.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.7.5 If the Race is interrupted after the chequered flag, the following procedure will apply:",
      "text": "7.8.7.5 If the Race is interrupted after the chequered flag, the following procedure will apply:\na) For all the riders to whom the chequered flag was shown before the interruption, a partial \nclassification will be established at the end of the last lap of the Race.\nb) For all the riders to whom the chequered flag was not shown before the interruption, a \npartial classification will be established at the end of the penultimate lap of the Race.\n\n71\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\nc) The complete classification will be established by combining both partial classifications as \nper the lap/time procedure.\n7�8�8 Change of Machine during a Competition",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.8.1 During any Competition, other than an attempt at a Record, no Machine may be exchanged for",
      "text": "7.8.8.1 During any Competition, other than an attempt at a Record, no Machine may be exchanged for \nanother unless permitted under these GCRs or any SRs.\n7�8�9 Radio Communication",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.9.1 Radio communications with riders is not allowed and will be classed as outside assistance.",
      "text": "7.8.9.1 Radio communications with riders is not allowed and will be classed as outside assistance.\n7�8�10          Scoring",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.10.1 The results for each competitor in each Competition will be determined by the allocation to that",
      "text": "7.8.10.1 The results for each competitor in each Competition will be determined by the allocation to that \ncompetitor of points in accordance with the following table:\nPLACEPOINTSPLACEPOINTS\n1251110\n220129\n318138\n417147\n516156\n615165\n714174\n813183\n912192\n1011201",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.10.2 If points are tied for any position in a Competition which is conducted over more than one Race,",
      "text": "7.8.10.2 If points are tied for any position in a Competition which is conducted over more than one Race, \nthe tying competitor who has the higher finishing position in the final Race of the Competition will \nbe awarded the position.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.10.3 If points are tied for any position in a Series, the tying competitor who has the greatest number of",
      "text": "7.8.10.3 If points are tied for any position in a Series, the tying competitor who has the greatest number of \nhigher placings in the Series will be awarded the position.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.10.4 An alternative points scoring system may be approved for an MA series Event.",
      "text": "7.8.10.4 An alternative points scoring system may be approved for an MA series Event.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.10.5 If a tie on points occurs for any position in an Event which is conducted over more than one",
      "text": "7.8.10.5 If a tie on points occurs for any position in an Event which is conducted over more than one \nleg, the tying competitor who has the higher finishing position in the final leg of the Event will be \nawarded the position.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.8.10.6 If a tie on points occurs for any position in a series, the tying competitor who has the greatest",
      "text": "7.8.10.6 If a tie on points occurs for any position in a series, the tying competitor who has the greatest \nnumber of higher placings in the series will be awarded the position.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 9 RACE EVENT PROTOCOLS: AUSTRALIAN HISTORIC ROAD RACE CHAMPIONSHIPS",
      "text": "7�9 RACE EVENT PROTOCOLS: AUSTRALIAN HISTORIC ROAD RACE CHAMPIONSHIPS\n7�9�1 Allocation of Numbers",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.9.1.1 The current Australian Championship title holding rider in every Historic Road Race",
      "text": "7.9.1.1 The current Australian Championship title holding rider in every Historic Road Race \nChampionship class is entitled to the number 1 plate for use in the capacity class for which the \ntitle is held.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.9.1.2 If the current champion in the respective Australian Championship class is not entered, or",
      "text": "7.9.1.2 If the current champion in the respective Australian Championship class is not entered, or \ndeclines to use the number 1 plate, the plate shall not be used by another competitor in that \nclass.\n7�9�2 Log Books",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.9.2.1 Machines entered in the Australian Historic Road Race Championships must have a log book",
      "text": "7.9.2.1 Machines entered in the Australian Historic Road Race Championships must have a log book \nissued by MA or be covered by GCR 7.4.3.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.9.2.2 Log book application forms are available on www.ma.org.au or from SCB.",
      "text": "7.9.2.2 Log book application forms are available on www.ma.org.au or from SCB.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.9.2.3 Log book applications may not be processed if lodged within six (6) weeks of the Championship.",
      "text": "7.9.2.3 Log book applications may not be processed if lodged within six (6) weeks of the Championship.\n\n72\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\nSubscribe to MNSW Calendar for NSW Events\nwww�motorcycling�com�au\n\n73\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "SECTION 7C: TECHNICAL REGULATIONS",
      "text": "SECTION 7C: TECHNICAL REGULATIONS",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 10 SOUND EMISSIONS",
      "text": "7�10 SOUND EMISSIONS",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.10.1.1 Sound testing must be carried out as per Appendix C: Sound Emissions & Fuel.",
      "text": "7.10.1.1 Sound testing must be carried out as per Appendix C: Sound Emissions & Fuel.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 11 FUEL",
      "text": "7�11             FUEL",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.11.1.1 Fuel for all Machines must be as per Appendix C: Sound Emissions & Fuel.",
      "text": "7.11.1.1 Fuel for all Machines must be as per Appendix C: Sound Emissions & Fuel.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.11.1.2 As of January 1st 2019, AV Gas is not acceptable for use in Historic Road Racing.",
      "text": "7.11.1.2  As of January 1st 2019, AV Gas is not acceptable for use in Historic Road Racing.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 12 ENGINES",
      "text": "7�12             ENGINES\n7�12�1          General",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.12.1.1 Engine capacity must not exceed 1300cc.",
      "text": "7.12.1.1 Engine capacity must not exceed 1300cc.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.12.1.2 Period 6 Formula Classes only: Oversize limit of 5% by cylinder boring only above the original",
      "text": "7.12.1.2 Period 6 Formula Classes only: Oversize limit of 5% by cylinder boring only above the original \nmanufacturer’s total engine capacity, provided that the upper limit of 1300cc is not exceeded. \nStroke to remain standard.\n7�12�2 Reciprocating Engines\n The formula for calculation of capacities and classes\n Cubic capacity = (D\n2\n x 3.1416 x C x N) \n                                                      4\n                    Where:        D = Bore in centimetres\n                                                         C = Stroke in centimetres\n                                                         N = Number of cylinders\n7�12�3 Rotary Engines:\n Cubic capacity = (Z x V) \n      N\n Where:     V = Capacity of each chamber, comprising the engine in cubic centimetres,\n                                                         N = Number of turns of the motor necessary to complete 1 cycle in a  \n  chamber, and\n                                        Z = Combustion cycles per revolution.\n7�12�4 Wankel System Engines with a Triangular Piston\n Cubic capacity =  2 x V x D\n                    Where:      V = Capacity of a single chamber,\n                                        D = The number of rotors.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.12.4.1 Wankel system engines are classified as 4-strokes.",
      "text": "7.12.4.1 Wankel system engines are classified as 4-strokes.\n7�12�5 Superchargers and Turbochargers",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.12.5.1 Superchargers and turbochargers may only be used as follows:",
      "text": "7.12.5.1 Superchargers and turbochargers may only be used as follows:\na) In Production Class or Improved Touring racing when fitted as factory equipment,\nb) The nominal cubic capacity of an engine as calculated under GCR 7.12.2, 7.12.3 or 7.12.4 \nthat is fitted with a supercharger or a turbocharger shall be multiplied by 2 for the purposes \nof engine classification,\nc) For Historic Road Race Period 2 Machines, when fitted with a supercharger as factory \nequipment.\n7�12�6 Engine Capacity Tolerances",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.12.6.1 The actual engine capacity of a Machine competing in a capacity class in Historic Road Race",
      "text": "7.12.6.1 The actual engine capacity of a Machine competing in a capacity class in Historic Road Race \nmay not exceed the prescribed capacity for that class by more than 5%.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 13 FRAMES AND PARTS",
      "text": "7�13 FRAMES AND PARTS",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.1.1 The use of titanium in the construction of the frame, front forks, handlebars, swinging arm,",
      "text": "7.13.1.1  The use of titanium in the construction of the frame, front forks, handlebars, swinging arm, \nswinging arm spindles and wheel spindles, is forbidden unless OEM. The use of light alloys for \nwheel spindles is also forbidden unless OEM. The use of titanium alloy nuts and bolts is allowed.\nFor up to date GCRs refer to the General Competition Rules page on the MA\nwebsite www�ma�org�au\n\n74\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.2 Compulsory\tModifications",
      "text": "7.13.2\t   Compulsory\tModifications",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.2.1 The following parts must be removed from any Machine before it may be entered in a",
      "text": "7.13.2.1 The following parts must be removed from any Machine before it may be entered in a \nCompetition:\na)      Headlamp,\nb) Tail lamp,\nc) Traffic indicators,\nd) Reflectors,\ne)      Horns,\nf) Rear vision mirrors,\ng) Centre, rear and side stands,\nh) Registration plate and label holder.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.2.2 Any sharp edges left by the removal of these components must be protected by a rolled edge or",
      "text": "7.13.2.2 Any sharp edges left by the removal of these components must be protected by a rolled edge or \nbeading of a minimum diameter of 3mm.\n7�13�3          General",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.1 All Machines must be fitted with a functioning engine cut out switch which must be either a",
      "text": "7.13.3.1 All Machines must be fitted with a functioning engine cut out switch which must be either a \nlanyard type or handlebar mounted.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.2 Plugs or caps which, if removed, permit the discharge of any lubricating, cooling or hydraulic",
      "text": "7.13.3.2 Plugs or caps which, if removed, permit the discharge of any lubricating, cooling or hydraulic \nfluids must be lock-wired or otherwise secured in the tightened position in a manner approved by \nthe Technical Officer. All high pressure oil lines to be secured by a pressure type fitting on Period \n4, 5, 6 and 7 Machines. Worm drive hose clips may be used on Period 1, 2 and 3 Machines.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.3 All hoses must be securely fitted and guarded to prevent contact with:",
      "text": "7.13.3.3 All hoses must be securely fitted and guarded to prevent contact with:\na) The ground, and\nb) Tyres or other moving parts over the full movement of the suspension.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.4 All engine, gearbox, fuel and radiator breather hoses and tubes, including the radiator overflow",
      "text": "7.13.3.4 All engine, gearbox, fuel and radiator breather hoses and tubes, including the radiator overflow \nbottle vent must:\na) Exhaust into the airbox to the rear of the intakes. The lower airbox breather tube must be \nblocked, or\nb) Exhaust into an oil catch tank with a minimum volume of 300ml which must be empty prior \nto each Competition.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.5 The only liquid coolants permitted are water and non-glycol coolants. Glycol and coolants",
      "text": "7.13.3.5 The only liquid coolants permitted are water and non-glycol coolants. Glycol and coolants \nmanufactured with glycol are not allowed.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.6 Handlebars",
      "text": "7.13.3.6       Handlebars       \na) The ends of the handlebars or twist grip sleeves must be securely plugged so as to present \na flush or rounded end,\nb) Handlebar levers must have ball ends with a minimum diameter of 16mm,\nc) Throttle controls must be self-closing.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.7 Heads with more than two valves per cylinder are prohibited in all periods unless originally fitted",
      "text": "7.13.3.7 Heads with more than two valves per cylinder are prohibited in all periods unless originally fitted \nby the manufacturer or were a proven period modification.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.8 Frame protection devices may be added to run lengthwise along the frame, providing they do not",
      "text": "7.13.3.8 Frame protection devices may be added to run lengthwise along the frame, providing they do not \nprotrude more than 80mm from the bodywork and are no more than 80mm in diameter.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.9 Where the exhaust system or swing arm does not shield the sprocket a chain guard must be fitted",
      "text": "7.13.3.9 Where the exhaust system or swing arm does not shield the sprocket a chain guard must be fitted \nin such a way to prevent trapping between the lower drive chain and the final drive sprocket at the \nrear wheel.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.13.3.10 All Period 4, 5, 6 and 7 Motorcycles with hydraulic brakes, may be fitted with braided brake lines.",
      "text": "7.13.3.10 All Period 4, 5, 6 and 7 Motorcycles with hydraulic brakes, may be fitted with braided brake lines.",
