    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "SECTION 7D: TECHNICAL REGULATIONS:",
      "text": "SECTION 7D: TECHNICAL REGULATIONS:",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7 14 ALL CLASSES",
      "text": "7�14 ALL CLASSES",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.1 The onus of proof of eligibility shall rest wholly upon the rider or entrant of the Machine. Service",
      "text": "7.14.1.1 The onus of proof of eligibility shall rest wholly upon the rider or entrant of the Machine. Service \nand parts manual publication dates are not proof of eligibility.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.2 Entrants must enter their Motorcycles at Historic Events quoting the year of manufacture.",
      "text": "7.14.1.2 Entrants must enter their Motorcycles at Historic Events quoting the year of manufacture.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.3 The eligibility and dating of Historic Motorcycles shall be considered in terms of major and minor",
      "text": "7.14.1.3 The eligibility and dating of Historic Motorcycles shall be considered in terms of major and minor \ncomponents and the period of the Motorcycle shall be the period of the latest major component.\n\n75\n7 HISTORIC ROAD RACE\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.4 For the purpose of these GCRs ‘year of manufacture’ is defined as the year in which:",
      "text": "7.14.1.4 For the purpose of these GCRs ‘year of manufacture’ is defined as the year in which:\na) For a road-based Machine, the Machine or its latest major component was first generally \navailable for sale and delivery to the purchaser,\nb) For a racing-based Machine, the year in which the Machine or the latest major component \nfirst appeared in open Competition.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.5 The dating of replicated major components is defined as the year of manufacture of the original",
      "text": "7.14.1.5 The dating of replicated major components is defined as the year of manufacture of the original \ncomponent being replicated.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.6 Major components are:",
      "text": "7.14.1.6 Major components are:\na) All engine and gearbox external castings,\nb)      Frames,\nc) Swinging arms,\nd)      Brakes,\ne) Forks and fork yokes.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.7 All other components shall be considered as minor components.",
      "text": "7.14.1.7 All other components shall be considered as minor components.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.8 Major components that were manufactured outside a specific period, but which are visually",
      "text": "7.14.1.8 Major components that were manufactured outside a specific period, but which are visually \nindistinguishable when assembled from period components shall be eligible for that period.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.9 Modifications to major components are allowed, providing such modifications are visually",
      "text": "7.14.1.9 Modifications to major components are allowed, providing such modifications are visually \nindistinguishable from modifications proven to have been used in the period.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.10 Components, whether major or minor, prohibited from use in any period will be deemed to be",
      "text": "7.14.1.10 Components, whether major or minor, prohibited from use in any period will be deemed to be \nprohibited from use in all earlier periods unless specifically permitted under these GCRs.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.11 Minor components may be modified or updated, provided that they remain visually compatible",
      "text": "7.14.1.11 Minor components may be modified or updated, provided that they remain visually compatible \nwith the period being depicted.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.12 Components manufactured outside the period are eligible, if permitted under these GCRs.",
      "text": "7.14.1.12 Components manufactured outside the period are eligible, if permitted under these GCRs.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.13 Fairings, streamlining and cosmetic components must be based on patterns known and used in",
      "text": "7.14.1.13 Fairings, streamlining and cosmetic components must be based on patterns known and used in \nthe period.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.14 Worm drive hose clamps on oil lines are permitted for Periods 1, 2 and 3 only.",
      "text": "7.14.1.14 Worm drive hose clamps on oil lines are permitted for Periods 1, 2 and 3 only.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.15 All Machines, whether standard or modified, must comply with the specifications of the period.",
      "text": "7.14.1.15 All Machines, whether standard or modified, must comply with the specifications of the period.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.16 For Period 6 & 7 production-based Machines where components/parts are no longer available",
      "text": "7.14.1.16 For Period 6 & 7 production-based Machines where components/parts are no longer available \nthrough the OEM of the Machine, the use of aftermarket components/parts is permitted under the \nfollowing conditions:\na) All aftermarket internal engine components/parts must be listed on the log book application \nfor the Machine and,\ni) be approved by the Australian Road Race Commission,\nii) be recorded in the log book for the Machine, and\niii) the onus of proving the component/part is within the intent of this rule and the class/\nPeriod is on the person seeking to prove it.\nb) The following components/parts are open,\ni) Wiring harness.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "7.14.1.17 The changing of a major component that will change the period or the class of a Motorcycle at an",
      "text": "7.14.1.17 The changing of a major component that will change the period or the class of a Motorcycle at an \nEvent is strictly forbidden.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
