      "text": "17.1.1          Matrix\nRoad Race\nHistoric Road Racing\nMinimoto\nMotocross & Supercross\nClassic Motocross\nEnduro, (Including Hard & Super)\nATV\nSpeedway\nDirt Track, Track & Flat Track\nClassic Dirt Track\nSupermoto & Minimotard\nTrial\nMinikhana\nHelmet\nC\nC\nC\nA\nA\nA\nB\nA\nA\nA\nC\nB\nB\nClothing\nA\nA\nA / E\n1\nC\n1\nC\nB\n1\nC\nA / C\n1\nA / C\n1 \nC\nA\nD\nC\nBack\n/\nChest Protection\nA/C\nA\nA\nB\n NA\nB\n NA\nB\n NA\nA\nA\nA\nA\nA\nNA\nB\nBody Armour\nNA\nNA\nB\n2\nC\nC\nC\nC / B\n1\nC\n1\nA / C\n1 \nB\nNA\nNA\nC\n1\nFootwear\nA\n1\nA\n1\nA\nE\nE\nE\nF\nB\nB \nD\nA / E\nF\nC\nGloves\nB\nB\nB\nB\nB\nB\nB\nA\nA \nB\nB\nC\nB\nNotes:\nMinimoto notes:1. E type only applicable to classes other than Elite Open.2. Only required when clothing type E is worn.\nATV notes:Soft roost protection alone is un-acceptable1. B type only applicable for Dirt Track.\nMinikhana notes:1. Only applicable for Minicross, Mini Enduro and Reliability events.\n1. Hair longer than shoulder length must be confined in the helmet or jacket.2. Body jewellery is to be removed or securely covered with tape prior to competition.3. Closed footwear must be worn in all pit areas (including pit lane, fuel control areas, work areas or parc ferme) at all times, and within any competition area for Minikhana.Road Race notes:1. Knee & boot scrapers that spark when dragged on the ground are forbidden.\nMotocross & Enduro notes:Motocross & Enduro notes:1. Protective clothing must not be loose or flapping.2. Mandatory for Junior competitors  and strongly recommended for all senior classes at Motocross and Enduro events. \nSoft roost protection \nis not permitted in Enduro events.Note: \nType C upper body protection \nmay be compulsory in Senior Competition classes via supplementary regulations in 2025. It will become mandatory for Senior Competition classes in Motocross and Enduro from 2026.\nSpeedway / Dirt Track & Track notes: Mechanics are encouraged to dress in team attire.1.Full upper-body armour must be worn under clothing type C.\n\n262\nAPP A: PROTECTIVE CLOTHING AND EQUIPMENT\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT\nb)c)\nd)",
