      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": "17.2.1 Matrix",
      "text": "17.2.1          Matrix\nFlags and Signals\n  Road Race\n  Historic Road Race\n  Motocross & Supercross\n  Classic MX & Classic Dirt Track\n  Enduro Special Tests\n  Hard & Super Enduro\n  ATV\n  Speedway\n  Dirt Track, Track & Flat Track\n  Supermoto\n  Trial\n  Minikhana\nDescriptions\nNational flag dropped or raised\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nStart of race.\nRed flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nRace or practice stopped prematurely. Competitors must slow down, must not overtake and must slowly proceed to the parc fermé, pits, or other areas as indicated to them by officials.The red flag will be used to signal the end of a demonstration.\nWhite flag with red cross waved\nx\nx\nx\nMedical staff on track, proceed with extreme caution at a very slow speed. Riders must roll each jump individually with no overtaking.\nWhite flag with red cross waved - Supercross \nonly  \nx\nMedical staff on the course, proceed with extreme caution. Riders must roll each jump individually with no overtaking until past the area of concern. Racing or accelerating in an unsafe manner in this area is prohibited.\nBlack flag held stationary and black board with rider's number\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nCompetitor with number indicated on black board must stop at the pits on the next lap.\nYellow flag held stationary\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nDanger, ride slowly, overtaking is forbidden.\nYellow flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nImmediate danger, slow down, prepare to stop, overtaking forbidden.\nYellow flag held stationary - Motocross\nx\nx\nx\nx\nDanger, ride cautiously.\nYellow flag waved - Motocross\nx\nx\nx\nx\nImmediate danger, prepare to stop, no overtaking. A significant reduction in speed must be observed; therefore, jumps should not be attempted (the waved yellow flag is superior to the stationary yellow flag).\nYellow flag waved - Supercross\nx\nDanger, ride cautiously, passing is allowed.\nYellow flag with red stripes held stationary\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nDeterioration of adhesion of the track.\nWhite flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nSlow moving intervention vehicle on track.\nBlue flag held stationary\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nCompetitor receiving flag is soon to be overtaken.\nBlue flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nCompetitor receiving flag is warned an overtake is imminent.\nGreen flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nCourse clear.\nLast lap board\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nIndicates the last lap has commenced.\nYellow flag with black diagonal cross - Speedway only \nx\nx\nIndicates the last lap has commenced.\nPurple flag\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nProtest flag for all Junior competitors.\nBlack and white chequered flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nFinish of race, qualifying or practice session.\nOne or two flashing yellow lights = Yellow flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nImmediate danger, slow down, prepare to stop, overtaking forbidden.\nGreen light = Green flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nCourse clear.\nRed light = Red flag waved\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nRace or practice stopped prematurely. Competitors must slow down, must not overtake and must slowly proceed to the parc fermé, pits, or other areas as indicated to them by officials.\nNo jump light = MX yellow flag\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nx\nDanger, overtaking forbidden, jumping forbidden.\nFlag signals may be supplemented by light signals as follows:\n\n267\nAPP C: SOUND EMISSION AND FUEL\n2026 MANUAL OF MOTORCYCLE SPORT",
